{
  "artifact_kind": "independent_static_finding_challenge",
  "id": "FIN-CAND-PAYROLL-001-ROOT-CHALLENGE-2026-10-21",
  "baseline": "c35816ecae49633674775dd32061c6ee92f94aaf",
  "reviewer": "/root coordinator",
  "finding_id": "FIN-CAND-PAYROLL-001",
  "status": "INDEPENDENT_SOURCE_CORROBORATION; RUNTIME_INTERLEAVING_UNVERIFIED",
  "severity_assessment": "HIGH_STATIC_WITH_QUALIFICATIONS_NO_SQL_REPRODUCTION; no severity escalation",
  "source_reasoning": "Independently read PayPayrollHandler.HandleAsync and TransitionPayrollHandler.HandleAsync. Payment checks Approved at PayPayrollHandler.cs:62-74, then computes payable lines before opening its DB transaction at 110-111; the transactional section locks treasury balance and writes movement, employee settlements, and Paid metadata at 118-163, but does not reread/conditionally update payroll run state. Cancellation reads the current status and validates the transition at TransitionPayrollHandler.cs:34-37, assigns target status at 54-57, then saves at 59-60 without an explicit shared run lock or transaction. PayrollRules.AssertTransition defines the allowed states at PayrollRules.cs:13-27. The payroll mapping shows unique period/idempotency keys but no configured rowversion/concurrency token at FalahDbContext.cs:460-477.",
  "plausible_interleavings": [
    "Pay reads Approved; cancel reads Approved and saves Cancelled; pay then enters transaction and persists Paid with the outflow/settlements without a state reread. Cancellation can return success although payment subsequently wins.",
    "Pay reads Approved; cancel reads Approved; pay commits payment and Paid; stale cancellation writes Cancelled afterward. In that schedule the final status may say Cancelled while treasury movement and employee settlements exist. Actual EF-generated update predicates and SQL Server scheduling were not executed, so final row outcome remains provider/runtime dependent."
  ],
  "counterevidence": [
    "PayPayroll is protected against a repeated same-run payout by a deterministic run idempotency key and transactional journal/treasury/settlement writes. This finding is not a duplicate-payment claim.",
    "Existing PayrollVerticalSliceTests cover sequential same-run replay and six concurrent pay requests (lines 208-258), but do not interleave cancellation with payment.",
    "The unique live-period index can constrain some schedules if a replacement run is inserted; no replacement run is assumed in the described schedule.",
    "EF tracking and SQL Server isolation details must be verified in an approved integration test; static source alone cannot prove actual winner/order."
  ],
  "root_cause": "The payable run state is read/validated outside the payment transaction, while cancellation independently reads and saves that same state without a shared row lock, conditional terminal-state update, or visible concurrency token; the money movement and run terminal status are not guarded by a single shared serialization boundary.",
  "impact": "Potentially contradictory audit/user state: cancellation can be acknowledged while payment settles, or a successful payment may coexist with a final Cancelled run state. No duplicated outflow is inferred.",
  "recommended_remediation": "Preserve a single terminal transition invariant by serializing payment and cancellation on the PayrollRun row or using a conditional state transition within the same database transaction as the side effects. The winner should determine one durable terminal state: cancellation success must imply no payroll movement/settlements; payment success must imply Paid plus exactly one movement and the matching settlements. Keep the existing same-run idempotency/journal and treasury balance lock.",
  "required_tests": [
    "On disposable SQL Server, force pay to pause after Approved read and force cancel to commit; resume pay. Verify the chosen winner policy and assert cancellation success never coexists with a payroll payment movement/settlement.",
    "Force cancellation to pause after reading Approved while payment commits; resume cancel. Assert stale cancellation is rejected/replayed and final status is Paid when payment won.",
    "Retain sequential and concurrent same-run pay tests and assert exactly one movement/journal and one settlement per eligible line.",
    "Inspect generated SQL/update predicates and assert concurrency/state guard is effective under actual provider isolation."
  ],
  "tests_executed": "NONE; read-only source/test inspection only",
  "owner_policy": "The required atomic terminal-state/accounting invariant is clear; user-facing winner/response semantics for an overlap should be explicitly selected by product owner if the API has not defined it.",
